From 2c3784865bd134625f428699a7850b143ab86c58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Moskowski <me@corpix.ru>
Date: Thu, 23 Apr 2026 21:45:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wireguard: add ranged magic headers and per-packet junk sizes

Allow advanced security configurations to describe H1-H4 magic
headers as single values or inclusive ranges, exposed through netlink
as NUL-terminated strings. Generate packet header values from those
ranges when sending and accept the configured ranges when receiving.

Add S3 and S4 device attributes for cookie reply and transport packet
junk sizes, and apply configured junk prefixes to those packet types
in addition to initiation and response packets.

Validate the full advanced security configuration before applying it,
including packet size limits and overlapping magic header ranges.
